Chromium Embedded Framework for Debian
=======================================

EXPERIMENTAL STATUS
-------------------

This package is EXPERIMENTAL and targeted for unstable/testing only.
It is NOT intended for stable releases at this time.

Binary Packages
---------------

This source package produces three binary packages:

  libcef138        - CEF shared library (libcef.so.138)
                     The version number (138) is the CEF major version.
                     See "CEF and Chromium Version Alignment" section below.

  libcef-dev       - Development files (headers, static libraries)
                     Depends on libcef138

  cef-resources    - Architecture-independent resources (PAK files, locales)
                     Required at runtime by CEF applications

depot_tools Build Dependency
----------------------------

This package requires Google's depot_tools to build. depot_tools is NOT
included in the source package and must be cloned manually before building:

  cd chromium-embedded-framework/
  git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git

depot_tools will be preserved across builds (not removed by 'dh clean').

See debian/README.source section "BUNDLED DEPENDENCIES JUSTIFICATION" for
technical details on why depot_tools cannot use system packages.

Note: depot_tools is only used during build. No depot_tools files are
installed to the system in the binary packages.

Package Structure and Chromium Integration
--------------------------------------------

**CEF Source Structure:**

This package maintains CEF source files in the cef/ subdirectory, NOT at
the package root:

  chromium-embedded-framework/
  ├── debian/              # Debian packaging files
  ├── cef/                 # CEF source code
  │   ├── tools/
  │   ├── include/
  │   └── ...
  └── chromium_*.orig.tar.xz  # Chromium tarball (parent directory)

**Why chromium is NOT bundled:**

Unlike qt6-webengine (which bundles Chromium in src/3rdparty/chromium/
because Qt upstream ships it that way), CEF upstream does NOT bundle
Chromium sources. CEF's build system expects to extract Chromium
separately at build time.

Therefore, chromium is a BUILD DEPENDENCY, not a component tarball.

**Build Process:**

This package uses Debian's chromium source tarball as input to CEF's
automate-git.py script. Build requirements:

  - 40GB disk space
  - 8GB RAM minimum
  - ~2 hours build time
  - Debian chromium tarball (chromium_*.orig.tar.xz)

**Development vs Final Packaging Modes:**

  Development mode (current):
    - Uses cached chromium tarball (../chromium_*.orig.tar.xz)
    - Enables rapid iteration without repeated downloads
    - debian/rules contains cache optimization logic

  Final mode (when Bug #893448 is resolved):
    - Will use chromium-source binary package
    - Automatic dependency resolution via apt
    - Cache logic removed from debian/rules

The packaging has been designed to make this migration straightforward -
only debian/rules needs updating to use chromium-source instead of the
local chromium tarball.

Packages Enabled
----------------

This CEF package enables functionality in:

  - obs-studio: Browser sources (currently disabled with -DENABLE_BROWSER=FALSE)
  - stremio-gtk: Entire application (currently cannot be packaged)
  - casparcg-server: HTTP support (currently disabled)
  - nageru: Potential improvements (to be investigated)

These packages have been waiting for CEF since 2018 (bug #915400).

Runtime Libraries and Configuration
-----------------------------------

**ANGLE Libraries (libEGL.so, libGLESv2.so):**

CEF includes Google's ANGLE libraries (Almost Native Graphics Layer Engine),
which provide OpenGL ES implementation over Vulkan. These are NOT the same
as system Mesa libraries (libegl1, libgles2).

To avoid conflicts with system Mesa libraries, the ANGLE libraries are
installed to a private directory:

  /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef/

The main CEF library (libcef.so) has RUNPATH set to find these libraries
automatically. This follows Debian policy for private shared libraries:

  https://wiki.debian.org/RpathIssue

Applications using CEF will automatically use the correct ANGLE libraries
without needing to set LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

**Chrome Sandbox:**

CEF includes chrome-sandbox for process isolation, installed at:

  /usr/lib/cef/chrome-sandbox

By default, this binary is NOT setuid root for security reasons. This means
sandbox support is disabled out of the box. Applications can work around
this by:

  1. Running with --no-sandbox flag, OR
  2. Manually enabling setuid (requires root):
     sudo chown root:root /usr/lib/cef/chrome-sandbox
     sudo chmod 4755 /usr/lib/cef/chrome-sandbox

**SwiftShader (Software Rendering):**

CEF includes SwiftShader for software Vulkan rendering when hardware
acceleration is unavailable. The Vulkan ICD configuration is installed to:

  /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/vk_swiftshader_icd.json

**Resource Files:**

CEF resource files (PAK files, locales, ICU data) are in the cef-resources
package, installed to:

  /usr/share/cef/

Applications need to set CefSettings.resources_dir_path to this location,
or symlink these files to the application's working directory.

CEF and Chromium Version Alignment
----------------------------------

CEF uses its own version numbering that is DISTINCT from the Chromium version.
The relationship is:

  CEF Version    CEF Branch    Chromium Version     Debian Status
  -----------    ----------    ----------------     -------------
  CEF 137        7444          142.0.7444.x         previous (142.0.7444.175)
  CEF 138        7499          143.0.7499.x         testing (143.0.7499.40)

**Why This Matters:**

This package (libcef138) was chosen specifically to align with Debian Chromium
in testing (143.0.7499.40). The CEF branch number (7499) corresponds to the
Chromium build number (143.0.**7499**.x).

**CEF Version Scheme:**

  - CEF version number (e.g., 138) is the CEF project's own major version
  - CEF branch number (e.g., 7499) maps directly to Chromium build number
  - Chromium version format: MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD.PATCH (e.g., 143.0.7499.40)
  - CEF branch 7499 = Chromium 143.0.7499.x

**Upstream CEF Branch in This Package:**

  - Git remote: upstream/7499
  - CHROMIUM_BUILD_COMPATIBILITY.txt: refs/tags/143.0.7499.110
  - This matches Debian Chromium testing (143.0.7499.40)

**Impact on Dependent Packages:**

Applications that depend on CEF should specify the CEF version they require:
  - stremio-gtk (uses libcef138) - now packagable with Chromium 143
  - obs-studio - compatible with libcef138

To update to a newer CEF version, both the CEF source and Chromium tarballs
must be updated to matching versions.

Security Updates
----------------

See README.security for the security update policy.

Debian Chromium Patch Integration
----------------------------------

This package applies Debian's Chromium patches to vanilla Chromium sources
before CEF uses them. This is a fundamental architectural decision.

**Why We Use Debian Chromium Patches:**

1. **System Integration**: Debian applies 300+ patches for system library
   integration (use_custom_libcxx=false, system LLVM, Node.js, etc.)

2. **Build Compatibility**: Fixes build issues with Debian's toolchain
   (GCC 14, LLVM 19, C++23 standard, SwiftShader compatibility)

**LLVM Usage Clarification - Two Different LLVM Purposes:**

This package uses LLVM in two completely separate contexts:

  1. **Compiler Toolchain (System LLVM-19)**
     - Used for *compiling* all Chromium/CEF C++ code
     - Provided by Debian's clang-19 package
     - Set via: clang_base_path="/usr/lib/llvm-19" in args.gn
     - This is the unbundled system LLVM

  2. **SwiftShader JIT (Bundled LLVM-16.0)**
     - Used by SwiftShader's Reactor library for *runtime JIT compilation*
     - Located at: third_party/swiftshader/third_party/llvm-16.0
     - This is a separate LLVM copy bundled inside Chromium's tarball
     - NOT related to system LLVM-19
     - The swiftshader-use-llvm-16.patch simply changes the path from
       the older bundled llvm-10.0 to the newer bundled llvm-16.0

  These are independent - system LLVM-19 compiles the code, while bundled
  LLVM-16.0 provides the JIT backend for SwiftShader's GPU emulation

3. **Security and Stability**: Includes Debian's security fixes and stability
   improvements

4. **Maintenance**: Avoids recreating Debian's work and ensures compatibility
   with Debian's Chromium package

**Required Tarballs:**

Both tarballs must be for the SAME Chromium version (e.g., 142.0.7444.162-1):

  - chromium_VERSION.orig.tar.xz (vanilla upstream Chromium)
  - chromium_VERSION-REVISION.debian.tar.xz (Debian packaging and patches)

**Patch Application Order in debian/rules:**

1. Extract vanilla Chromium tarball
2. Extract Debian Chromium packaging tarball
3. Apply Debian patches (debianization/, fixes/, system/)
4. Apply CEF patches (debian/patches/*.cef.patch via quilt)
5. Run CEF automate-git.py with pre-patched Chromium

**Key Debian Chromium Patches Applied:**

  - use_custom_libcxx=false (use system libc++ instead of bundled)
  - swiftshader-use-llvm-16.patch (LLVM compatibility)
  - absl-optional.patch (workaround for Clang bug #50248 with system libstdc++)
  - System library integration (Node.js, LLVM, toolchain)
  - C++23 standard compliance fixes

**Version Synchronization:**

CEF and Chromium versions must match. When updating Chromium:
1. Update both .orig.tar.xz and .debian.tar.xz to same version
2. Update debian/rules tarball extraction paths
3. Test patch application (Debian patches may need updates)
4. Test CEF build with new Chromium version

Patch Documentation
-------------------

This section documents all patches applied during the build process, grouped
by category and application order.

**Patch Application Order:**

1. CEF Patches (applied via quilt to CEF source - debian/patches/*.cef.patch)
2. Debian Chromium Patches (extracted from chromium_*.debian.tar.xz)
3. CEF Chromium Patches (applied manually to Chromium source - debian/patches/chromium/*.chromium.patch)

**CEF Patches (debian/patches/):**

Applied via quilt to CEF source files before Chromium extraction:

  0001-debian-patcher-skip-logic.cef.patch
    Skips CEF's patch application logic when DEBIAN_BUILD=1 environment
    variable is set. Allows Debian packaging to handle patch management.

  0002-use-system-clang.cef.patch
    Configures CEF to use Debian's system clang instead of downloading
    bundled LLVM/Clang toolchain.

  0003-create-reclient-stub.cef.patch
    Creates empty stub for reclient (remote execution tool) since Debian
    builds locally without Google's distributed build infrastructure.

  0004-patch-gn-for-exec-script.cef.patch
    Patches GN configuration to handle exec_script() calls correctly in
    Debian build environment.

  0005-skip-gclient-revert-debian.cef.patch
    Prevents gclient from reverting local modifications made by Debian
    patches during sync operations.

  0006-skip-chromium-checkout-debian.cef.patch
    Skips Chromium source checkout from Git (uses Debian tarball instead)
    when DEBIAN_BUILD=1 is set.

  0007-allow-optimize-webui-false-debian.cef.patch
    Allows optimize_webui=false GN argument to work correctly (needed
    because Debian's Node.js configuration differs from Chromium's bundled).

  0008-add-locale-stub-for-protoc-gen-js.cef.patch
    Creates minimal std::locale stub implementation to work around linking
    issues with protoc-gen-js when using system libc++.

  0009-update-cef-mac-frame-patch.cef.patch
    Updates CEF's macOS frame handling patch to apply correctly against
    Debian's pre-patched Chromium source.

  0010-add-rust-toolchain-stub.cef.patch
    Creates stub third_party/rust-toolchain/VERSION file after gclient sync
    to satisfy rust.gni requirements when using Debian's system rustc.

**CEF Chromium Patches (debian/patches/chromium/):**

Applied manually to Chromium source after extraction:

  0007-debian-tarball-deps.chromium.patch
    Disables gclient hooks that query Git history (lastchange, gpu_lists_version,
    etc.) by adding 'condition': 'not source_tarball' guards. Git metadata
    doesn't exist in Debian tarballs.

  0008-debian-tarball-gclient-toplevel.chromium.patch
    Modifies gclient configuration to work with Debian tarball structure
    (no top-level .gclient file).

  0009-disable-optimize-images-when-optimize-webui-false.chromium.patch
    Ensures optimize_images follows optimize_webui setting (both must be
    false when using Debian's Node.js).

  0010-fix-dri-pkg-config-debian.chromium.patch
    Fixes pkg-config detection for DRI/Mesa libraries in Debian's multi-arch
    environment.

  0013-remove-rust-nightly-flags-debian.chromium.patch
    Removes -Zallow-features flag and other nightly-only Rust compiler flags
    that are incompatible with Debian's stable rustc.

  0015-network-isolation-disable-google-storage-downloads.chromium.patch
    Disables automatic downloads from Google Cloud Storage for network
    isolation resources during Debian builds.

  0016-skip-protoc-gen-js.chromium.patch
    Modifies protoc-gen-js BUILD.gn to add --undefined linker flags for
    missing std::locale symbols (works with stub from patch 0008).

  0016-protoc-gen-js-gn-action-stub.chromium.patch
    Alternative approach: stubs out protoc-gen-js GN action entirely
    (not currently used).

  0017-disable-panic-immediate-abort.chromium.patch
    Disables panic=immediate-abort Rust flag that's incompatible with Debian's
    rustc panic runtime configuration.

  0017-make-siso-import-optional.chromium.patch
    Makes siso (Google's build system) import optional to prevent errors when
    not available in Debian environment.

  0018-rust-clanglib.chromium.patch
    Patches build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni to use system clang's resource directory
    for bindgen operations. Fixes libclang detection issues.
    NOTE: Also present in Debian Chromium's fixes/ (duplicate).

  0018-skip-gcs-deps-when-source-tarball.chromium.patch
    Skips dependency downloads from Google Cloud Storage when building from
    source tarballs (identified by 'source_tarball' condition).

  0019-bindgen-libclang-abspath.chromium.patch
    Sets absolute path to system libclang for bindgen, ensuring correct
    library detection in Debian's multi-arch environment.

  0019-skip-test-fonts.chromium.patch
    Skips test_fonts download hook (fonts would be downloaded from GCS,
    not needed for Debian builds).

  0020-skip-nodejs-version-check.chromium.patch
    Disables strict Node.js version check to allow Debian's system Node.js
    version (may differ from Chromium's pinned version).

  0021-disable-warning-suppression-mappings.chromium.patch
    Disables Chromium's warning suppression file mappings to prevent build
    system from creating CLANG_MVERS symlinks (conflicts with Debian's
    system clang setup).

  0022-libcpp-headers.chromium.patch
    Removes references to bundled libc++ headers from BUILDCONFIG.gn since
    we use system libc++ (use_custom_libcxx=false).
    NOTE: Similar to Debian Chromium's debianization/libcpp.patch (duplicate).

**Debian Chromium Patches (from chromium_*.debian.tar.xz):**

Extracted and applied automatically by debian/rules during build. These patches
are maintained by the Debian Chromium team and grouped into three categories:

  debianization/ (6 patches)
    Patches to adapt Chromium build system for Debian packaging:
    - master-preferences (default browser settings)
    - manpage (manual page generation)
    - optimization (build optimization flags)
    - quic (QUIC protocol Debian-specific config)
    - libcpp.patch (use system libc++ headers)
    - etc.

  fixes/ (20 patches)
    Bug fixes and compatibility patches:
    - C++23 standard compliance fixes
    - GCC 14 compatibility
    - absl-optional.patch (workaround Clang bug #50248 with system libstdc++)
    - LLVM/Clang compatibility fixes
    - rust-clanglib.patch (DUPLICATE of CEF's 0018-rust-clanglib.chromium.patch)
    - Architecture-specific fixes (ppc64el, riscv64, etc.)
    - etc.

  system/ (6 patches)
    System library integration patches:
    - zlib, libpng, freetype, harfbuzz, lcms2, openjpeg2
    - Replaces bundled libraries with Debian's system libraries

  Total: ~32 patches maintained by Debian Chromium team

**Duplicate Patch Handling:**

Two patches exist in BOTH Debian Chromium and CEF:

  1. rust-clanglib.patch (Debian Chromium fixes/) ==
     0018-rust-clanglib.chromium.patch (CEF)

     Both patch build/rust/rust_bindgen.gni to fix bindgen libclang detection.
     CEF's version is applied AFTER Debian's, so CEF's version takes precedence
     if they differ.

  2. libcpp.patch (Debian Chromium debianization/) ~=
     0022-libcpp-headers.chromium.patch (CEF)

     Both remove bundled libc++ header references. Similar purpose but
     different implementations. Both are applied (Debian first, then CEF).

These duplicates are maintained to ensure CEF builds correctly even if Debian
Chromium's patches change or are removed in future versions.

**Patch File Organization:**

  debian/patches/
  ├── 0001-0010*.cef.patch       (CEF patches, applied via quilt)
  ├── chromium/                  (CEF Chromium patches, applied manually)
  │   └── 00XX-*.chromium.patch
  └── series                     (lists CEF patches only, not chromium/)

The series file controls quilt patch application order and contains ONLY CEF
patches (0001-0010). Chromium patches in chromium/ subdirectory are applied
manually by debian/rules and are NOT listed in the series file.

